---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Now" description="What James Nguyen is working on, building, learning, and looking for right now.">
    <section class="now-header">
        <h1>Now</h1>
        <p class="updated">Updated October 2026</p>
        <p class="intro">
            What I'm doing these days. Not a resume, not a project list; just where my time goes.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Working</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Role</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Finance &amp; Operations Analyst and internal developer at Day &amp; Night Solar,
                    a commercial solar and energy-storage contractor.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Building</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    I'm the sole developer of the internal operations platform (Python + SQLite):
                    data pipelines, QuickBooks import automation that fails closed, confidence-scored
                    reconciliation, document extraction, and a governed AI agent workflow.
                    Concepts only; the code is private.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Building on my own time</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Atlas</span>
                <span class="now-value">A local-first personal data lakehouse.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Watt in Tarnation</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    A garage solar lab. The next step is a power meter, not a battery.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Solar compute</span>
                <span class="now-value">A solar-powered compute demonstrator. Early.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Cinemetrics</span>
                <span class="now-value">Still shipping to it.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Learning</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Measuring</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Measuring before tuning: local LLM inference on a 12 GB GPU.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Queues</span>
                <span class="now-value">Queue semantics for AI agents.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Electronics</span>
                <span class="now-value">Datasheet-first electronics.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Writing</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Lessons</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Short <a href="/blog#lessons">lessons</a> from what breaks.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Reading and using</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Tools</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Claude Code, MCP, llama.cpp, Ollama, ComfyUI, SQLite, pandas, pytest.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>The plan</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Now</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Hold automation to one rule: no check ships without a caller, a schedule, a
                    consequence when it fails, and an owner. A check nobody calls is a false
                    sense of safety, not a safeguard.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Next</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Take "one store, one fact, one owner" out of this one platform and make it a
                    pattern I carry into whatever I build next, not a rule that only applies here.
                    Publish the public reconciliation demo so the finance-automation work has
                    proof a stranger can run, not just a description.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Later</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Go deeper on the formal side of data engineering — distributed systems,
                    database internals, the theory behind the verification habits I've mostly
                    learned by getting burned. The instinct is there; I want the fundamentals
                    under it.
                </span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Standard</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Keep writing the lessons as they happen, not after. A rule I can't trace back
                    to the day it cost me something doesn't go on the list.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="now">
        <h2>Looking for</h2>
        <ul class="now-list">
            <li>
                <span class="now-label">Roles</span>
                <span class="now-value">
                    Full-time roles where accounting, data, and code meet: finance systems, analytics
                    engineering, data and automation engineering, and internal tools.
                    <a href="mailto:jamesmnguyen704@outlook.com">Email me</a>.
                </span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="now-footer">
        This is a now page. The idea comes from
        <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" rel="noopener">Derek Sivers</a>.
    </p>
</Layout>

<style>
    .now-header { margin: 4rem 0 2rem; max-width: 780px; }
    .now-header h1 { font-size: 3rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .updated {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .intro {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: #ddd;
    }

    section { margin: 3rem 0; max-width: 780px; }
    section h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .now-list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 0;
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        max-width: 780px;
    }
    .now-list li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;
    }
    .now-label {
        color: #888;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        padding-top: 0.15rem;
    }
    .now-value { color: #ddd; line-height: 1.6; }
    .now-value a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: none;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(217, 163, 62, 0.35);
    }

    .now-footer {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin-top: 3rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .now-footer a {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        text-decoration: none;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .now-footer a:hover { color: var(--text-color); }

    @media (max-width: 500px) {
        .now-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
    }
</style>
